  "findings": {
    "arm": "sunit-equations",
    "lemma": "For A with all pairwise sums S-smooth and any a>b in A, x |-> (a+x, b+x) injects A\\{a,b} into the solutions of U-W=a-b in positive S-smooth U,W. Hence g(k) <= 2 + min_{a>b in A} N_S(a-b).",
    "implication_direction": "S-unit solution-count bound ==> bound on g(k) ==> Erdos #126. NOT reversible.",
    "strongest_applicable_theorem": "Evertse 1984: ax+by=1 with x,y S-units of K has <= 3*7^{d+2s} solutions (d=[K:Q], s=#S incl. infinite places, a,b in K* fixed). Over Q with |S|=k primes: s=k+1, bound 3*7^{2k+3}.",
    "rank_based_alternative": "Beukers-Schlickewei 1996 Thm 1.1: <= 2^{8r+8} for the Q-closure of a rank-r subgroup of (C*)^2. Our solution set sits in a rank <= 2k+1 group, giving 2^{16k+16}, worse than Evertse here.",
    "classical_bound": "Erdos-Turan 1934: g(k) < 3*2^{k-1}; Erdos-Suranyi: g(k) <= 2^k.",
    "verdict": "Standard S-unit bounds are quantitatively too weak by an exponential factor. At k=7 Evertse gives g(7) <= 6.98e14 while the elementary 1960 argument gives 128 and the measured solution count of the very equation being bounded is 96.",
    "what_would_suffice": "Improving the base 49 = 7^2 in Evertse's S-unit bound over Q to anything below 2 already beats the 1934/1960 bound via this lemma; improving it to exp(o(s)) settles Erdos #126.",
    "is_that_plausible": "Best known lower bound for S-unit equation solution counts is Erdos-Stewart-Tijdeman exp((4+o(1))(s/log s)^{1/2}), which is exp(o(s)). Measured Stormer counts N_S(1) = 1,4,10,23,40,68,108,167 for k=1..8 fit ~k^3.2, i.e. polynomial. Nothing known contradicts exp(o(k)).",
    "oracle_check": "N_S(1) reproduced Lehmer/Stormer published counts exactly for k=1..8 inside the box 10^14.",
    "not_settled": "No improvement on g(k) is proved here. The lemma reduces #126 to an open quantitative question about unit equations; it does not answer it."
  }
}